<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eleftherios Venizelos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1864–1936</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eleftherios Venizelos was a Cretan politician who led the campaign for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>'s union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and became Prime Minister of Greece in 1910. He doubled the country's territory in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-wars">Balkan Wars</a>. Clashing with King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-i">Constantine I</a> over entry into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, he set up a rival government in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Thessaloniki</a> in 1916, and led Greece several times until 1933.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eleftherios-venizelos.jpg" alt="Eleftherios Venizelos" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photoprint copyrighted by Harris &amp;amp; Ewing (No known restrictions on publication) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eleftherios_Venizelos_1919_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
